From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] workqueue: a cancel in a frozen workqueue leaves no stale pending pwq

The battery level of the GO Ultra stood still for good after some
hibernations (and could after an s2idle sleep): the RK818 driver's work on
its freezable ordered workqueue "rk818-bat" stayed inactive, active=0, also
after a charger plug requeued it.

The way there: the driver's 5 s timer fires after freeze_workqueues_begin()
and before the driver's suspend callback (some 0.5 s in a hibernation: the
image preallocation). The work item is queued on the frozen workqueue: the
node's nr_active allows nothing (max 0), the pwq goes onto
nna->pending_pwqs and the work item onto pwq->inactive_works. The suspend
callback's cancel_delayed_work_sync() takes the work item off
inactive_works but leaves the pwq on pending_pwqs. Only a work item that
retires on the node (node_activate_pending_pwq()) drops a pwq without
inactive work items from there, and none does: nothing ran. At the thaw,
wq_adjust_max_active() finds no inactive work item to activate. From then
on pwq_tryinc_nr_active() sees the pwq still pending and keeps every new
work item inactive behind it ("don't jump the line"), for good.

Reproduced on the board with a test module (a freezable ordered workqueue,
queue_work() + cancel_work_sync() in a device's suspend callback, one
s2idle sleep with an RTC wake): STALL after the wake, OK with this patch.

try_to_grab_pending() now drops the pwq from pending_pwqs when it takes
its last inactive work item.
---
--- a/kernel/workqueue.c
+++ b/kernel/workqueue.c
@@ -1883,6 +1883,33 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * pwq_drop_pending - Drop an idle pwq from its wq_node_nr_active's pending list
+ * @pwq: pool_workqueue that has just lost an inactive work item
+ *
+ * A pwq that waits on $nna stays on $nna->pending_pwqs until a retiring work
+ * item finds it in node_activate_pending_pwq(). If its last inactive work
+ * item is cancelled while $nna allows no active work item at all (a frozen
+ * freezable workqueue: max 0), no work item retires on $nna afterwards and
+ * the stale entry stays: after the thaw, pwq_tryinc_nr_active() keeps every
+ * new work item of @pwq behind it and the workqueue never runs again. Drop
+ * it at the cancel. Called with @pwq->pool->lock held.
+ */
+static void pwq_drop_pending(struct pool_workqueue *pwq)
+{
+	struct wq_node_nr_active *nna = wq_node_nr_active(pwq->wq, pwq->pool->node);
+
+	lockdep_assert_held(&pwq->pool->lock);
+
+	if (!nna || !list_empty(&pwq->inactive_works) ||
+	    list_empty(&pwq->pending_node))
+		return;
+
+	raw_spin_lock(&nna->lock);
+	list_del_init(&pwq->pending_node);
+	raw_spin_unlock(&nna->lock);
+}
+
+/**
  * node_activate_pending_pwq - Activate a pending pwq on a wq_node_nr_active
  * @nna: wq_node_nr_active to activate a pending pwq for
  * @caller_pool: worker_pool the caller is locking
@@ -2155,6 +2182,9 @@
 
 		list_del_init(&work->entry);
 
+		if (work_data & WORK_STRUCT_INACTIVE)
+			pwq_drop_pending(pwq);
+
 		/*
 		 * work->data points to pwq iff queued. Let's point to pool. As
 		 * this destroys work->data needed by the next step, stash it.
